    "“%@” was not found on your PATH. Install it, then try again." : {
      "comment" : "A message that appears in a dialog box when the user tries to run a tool that's not installed. The argument is the name of the tool.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "**Git.** Sevinda pushes a branch only when you ask, using your own remotes and git credentials." : {

    },
    "**GitHub.** If the GitHub CLI (`gh`) is installed, Sevinda uses it with your own GitHub sign-in to show a branch's pull request and checks, and to create pull requests you ask for. When you ask for a workspace's GitHub avatar, Sevinda downloads the repository owner's public picture from github.com." : {

    },
    "**Markdown files.** When a Markdown file you open shows images from the web, they load from their addresses, as in a browser." : {

    },
    "**Updates.** This version of Sevinda does not check for updates. When a later version does, this policy will name the address it asks and how to turn the check off." : {

    },
    "**Usage limits.** For each Claude or Codex login whose limits Sevinda shows, it asks Anthropic (`api.anthropic.com`) or OpenAI (`chatgpt.com`) with that login's own token, now and then and when you click refresh. Only the token (and the Codex account ID) is sent; the reply holds percentages and reset times." : {

