    },
    "Sevinda is provided “as is” and “as available”, without warranties of any kind, express or implied, including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose and non-infringement. We do not promise that Sevinda is free of errors, runs without interruption or works with every future version of the agents it starts." : {

    },
    "Sevinda never changes your own Claude Code or Codex sign-ins or settings. Its Claude hooks are passed to each session it starts, not installed in your settings. The one thing it can add to `~/.claude` is its orchestration guide in `~/.claude/skills`, and only if you turn that on in Settings → Agents." : {

    },
    "Sevinda reads credentials into memory only for the request that needs them, and never prints or logs them." : {

    },
    "Sevinda shows Markdown, code, text, images and PDFs. Open this file in its default app instead." : {
      "comment" : "A description of what to do if the file viewer can't display the file.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "Sevinda starts programs you install yourself: Claude Code, Codex, git, the GitHub CLI and your shell. Your use of them, and of the accounts behind them, is governed by their providers' own terms (for example Anthropic, OpenAI and GitHub). Sevinda does not provide those accounts or plans." : {

    },
    "Sevinda works on your Mac. There are no Sevinda servers and no Sevinda account, and Sevinda collects no analytics, telemetry or crash reports. This policy lists what Sevinda reads, what it stores and the few connections it makes." : {

